---
import PublicLayout from '../../../layouts/PublicLayout.astro';
import GuidePdfPreview from '../../../components/guides/GuidePdfPreview.astro';
import GuidePageGallery from '../../../components/guides/GuidePageGallery.astro';
import {kinds,planning,mealCategories,team,issues,familyPrompt} from '../../../../scripts/lib/dinner-guide-content.mjs';
const pdf='/downloads/family-dinner-system.pdf';
const images=[1,2,3,4].map(n=>`/images/guides/dinner-guide-page-${n}.webp`);
const art=(name:string)=>`/assets/icons/ofc/guides/dinner/${name}.png`;
---
<PublicLayout title="The Family Dinner System: Meal Planning and Sharing Dinner Jobs" description="Stop making every dinner decision yourself. A free practical guide to Full, Short and Zero dinner nights, family favorites, shared mealtime jobs and a four-page printable." width="full" ogType="article">
<div class="omc-guide text-[#545454]">
<section class="px-5 py-9 sm:px-8 sm:py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-sm font-medium"><a href="/guides" class="underline underline-offset-4">Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true" class="mx-2">/</span>The Family Dinner System</nav>
<header class="mx-auto mt-9 max-w-[52rem] text-center">
<p class="eyebrow">MEAL PLANNING · FAMILY OWNERSHIP</p>
<h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-[clamp(2.4rem,6vw,4.25rem)] leading-[1.09] tracking-tight">Dinner shouldn't be one more thing Mom carries alone.</h1>
<p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-[42rem] text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.8] sm:text-lg">You don't need 30 new recipes. You need dinners that fit your actual week, a short list of family favorites, and people who know which part of the work they own.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-xs text-[#777]">Free practical guide · Four-page illustrated PDF · Uses our existing free dinner tools</p>
</header>
<div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-8 border-t-[5px] border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6 sm:p-10 md:grid-cols-[1.15fr_.85fr]">
<div><p class="eyebrow">FREE PRINTABLE · FOUR US LETTER PAGES</p><h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl leading-tight">The Family Dinner System</h2>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-sm leading-[1.8] sm:text-base">Plan the nights before the food, write your go-to dinners, choose four family roles and handle nights when the plan falls apart.</p>
<ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm leading-relaxed"><li>✓ Full, Short or Zero: a dinner that fits every night</li><li>✓ A reusable family favorites worksheet</li><li>✓ Clear Dinner Team jobs from planning through cleanup</li></ul>
<a href={pdf} download="OMC-Family-Dinner-System.pdf" class="btn-primary mt-7">Download the free PDF</a>
<p class="mt-2 text-xs text-[#6f6a65]">Four pages · Email requested on first download · Marketing optional</p></div>
<div class="py-5"><GuidePdfPreview pdf={pdf} images={images} title="The Family Dinner System"/></div>
</div>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="mt-8 border-t border-[#ded8d2] pt-5"><p class="label mb-3 text-[#6f6a65]">IN THIS GUIDE</p>
<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap sm:gap-3">
<a class="guide-anchor" href="#planning">Plan dinner</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#favorites">Favorite dinners</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#team">The Dinner Team</a><a class="guide-anchor" href="#problems">When plans change</a><a class="guide-anchor max-sm:col-span-2" href="#printable">Free printable</a></div></nav>
</div></section>
<section id="planning" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">01 · PLAN NIGHTS FIRST</p><h2 class="section-heading">Three kinds of night. No more dinner guessing.</h2>
<p class="section-lede">First look at the real family schedule. Label nights by the time and energy you have. Then choose four or five realistic dinners and leave room for leftovers and flexibility. This is the same method as our free Weekly Dinner Planner.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">{kinds.map(([icon,name,time,detail])=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><img src={art(icon)} alt="" width="70" height="70" loading="lazy" class="size-[70px] object-contain"/><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-2xl">{name} night</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm font-semibold">{time}</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<h3 class="mt-11 font-serif text-3xl">The 20-minute family dinner check.</h3>
<div class="mt-7 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{planning.map(([icon,title,detail],i)=><article class="border-t-[5px] border-[#D4DFC4] bg-white p-6"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src={art(icon)} alt="" width="60" height="60" loading="lazy" class="size-[60px] object-contain"/><span class="font-serif text-2xl">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span></div><h4 class="mt-3 font-serif text-xl">{title}</h4><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-9 bg-[#CDDDE1]/35 p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Make your actual plan with the free tool.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">The worksheet explains the method. Our Weekly Dinner Planner handles the days, dinner ownership, backup meals and grocery list in one printable.</p><a href="/meal-planner" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Open the free Weekly Dinner Planner</a></div>
</div></section>
<section id="favorites" class="bg-[#D4DFC4]/20 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">02 · LESS DECIDING</p><h2 class="section-heading">Build a shortlist of dinners you already know.</h2>
<p class="section-lede">The easiest meal rotation is made from what your family already likes. Page two of the printable has twelve blank lines, grouped into Full, Short and Zero nights. Use these familiar dinner families to get started.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{mealCategories.map(([icon,title])=><article class="flex items-center gap-4 border-t-[5px] border-[#D4DFC4] bg-white p-5"><img src={art(icon)} alt="" width="60" height="60" loading="lazy" class="size-[60px] shrink-0 object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3></article>)}</div>
<p class="mt-7 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Make sure at least two are true Zero-night options. Frozen meals, sandwiches or leftovers count. And check what's already in the fridge and pantry before adding anything to the shopping list.</p>
<div class="mt-6 text-sm"><a href="/resources/grocery-list-from-meal-plan" class="font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Learn how to make a grocery list anyone can shop from</a></div>
</div></section>
<section id="team" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">03 · SHARE THE WHOLE JOB</p><h2 class="section-heading">Dinner is a team job, including the thinking.</h2>
<p class="section-lede">We use the same four roles as our April Organized Family Club resource. The Dinner Captain owns the plan, not just the cooking. Everyone else has one part they can learn and repeat.</p>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">{team.map(([icon,title,who,detail])=><article class="grid gap-4 border-t-[5px] border-[#F1D8A8] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6 sm:grid-cols-[72px_1fr]"><img src={art(icon)} alt="" width="66" height="66" loading="lazy" class="size-[66px] object-contain"/><div><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">{title}</h3><p class="mt-1 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">{who}</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">{detail}</p></div></article>)}</div>
<div class="mt-9 grid gap-6 bg-[#CDDDE1]/35 p-7 sm:p-9 md:grid-cols-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">AT THE FAMILY MEETING</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl">Start with one dinner.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Choose an easy meal and fill in the four roles on page three. Work through it together, then keep the team for the next meal.</p></div><div><p class="font-serif text-xl leading-[1.5]">“{familyPrompt}”</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Adults still manage heat, knives, heavy dishes, raw meat and allergy decisions. Children learn safe jobs with supervision. Single-parent families can start with one child-owned job, without pretending another adult is available.</p></div></div>
<a href="/resources/kids-helping-with-dinner" class="mt-5 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">See safe dinner jobs for kids by age</a>
</div></section>
<section id="problems" class="bg-[#E8D2D6]/20 px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">04 · REAL FAMILY NIGHTS</p><h2 class="section-heading">When dinner doesn't go according to plan.</h2><p class="section-lede">Don't scrap the whole system over one late practice or a missing ingredient. Swap dinners, keep the handoff visible and make the next night easier.</p>
<div class="mt-8 space-y-3">{issues.map(([icon,title,fix])=><article class="grid gap-4 border-l-4 border-[#E8D2D6] bg-white p-5 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.4fr]"><div class="flex items-center gap-3"><img src={art(icon)} alt="" width="50" height="50" loading="lazy" class="size-[50px] shrink-0 object-contain"/><h3 class="font-serif text-xl">{title}</h3></div><p class="text-sm leading-[1.8]">{fix}</p></article>)}</div>
</div></section>
<section id="printable" class="px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
<p class="eyebrow">PRINT AND PRACTICE</p><h2 class="section-heading">Four pages. One dinner system.</h2><p class="section-lede">The worksheet teaches the system and gives your family a place to write its own favorites and first Dinner Team. The free planner remains the place to fill out each real week.</p>
<div class="mt-9 border border-[#ded8d2] bg-white p-7 sm:p-9"><GuidePageGallery images={images} title="The Family Dinner System"/><div class="mt-8 text-center"><a href={pdf} download="OMC-Family-Dinner-System.pdf" class="btn-primary">Download the free PDF</a><p class="mt-2 text-xs">Four US Letter pages · Email requested for first download</p></div></div>
<div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="border-t-4 border-[#CDDDE1] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Choose what to eat and buy.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">Use the free Weekly Dinner Planner for dinners, owners and the grocery list.</p><a href="/meal-planner" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Free Weekly Dinner Planner</a></div><div class="border-t-4 border-[#D4DFC4] bg-[#FBF7F1] p-6"><h3 class="font-serif text-2xl">Keep cleanup shared, too.</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-[1.8]">The Family Kitchen Reset shows everyone exactly what to do after the meal.</p><a href="/guides/family-kitchen-reset/" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Family Kitchen Reset guide</a></div></div>
<div class="mt-10 bg-[#FBF7F1] p-7"><p class="eyebrow">WANT THE DINNER PREPARED FOR YOU?</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl">One prepared meal. Your family's Dinner Team.</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-[1.8]">Organized Family Club's April resource gives members a prepared dinner with ingredients and directions, plus personalized Dinner Captain, Ingredients Checker, Table Captain and Cooking Lead assignments. Printed resources come in the mail.</p><a href="/club" class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Explore the Organized Family Club</a></div>
</div></section></div>
<style>
.omc-guide{font-family:Montserrat,Arial,sans-serif}.omc-guide section[id]{scroll-margin-top:110px}
.omc-guide .eyebrow{font-size:.72rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase}
.omc-guide .section-heading{max-width:800px;margin-top:14px;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(2rem,4.6vw,3.15rem);line-height:1.16;letter-spacing:-.025em}
.omc-guide .section-lede{max-width:700px;margin-top:16px;font-size:1.06rem;line-height:1.8}
.omc-guide .guide-anchor{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:48px;padding:10px 13px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d8d1cb;border-radius:3px;color:#545454;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.25;text-align:center;text-decoration:none}
.omc-guide .guide-anchor:hover{background:#CDDDE1}.omc-guide .guide-anchor:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #545454;outline-offset:2px}
@media(min-width:640px){.omc-guide .guide-anchor{min-height:44px;padding:9px 14px;font-size:13px}}
</style>
</PublicLayout>
